 ## Known gaps / follow-ups
 
 - **`interp_depth`'s limit branch is not reachable through the current grammar**, so no test pins it. Deep nesting needs a text literal *inside* an interpolated expression, and the outer lexer resolves escapes before the parser sees the literal — so the quotes that would delimit the inner literal have already become ordinary characters, and the inner source re-lexes into something that is not an expression. `edge_a_substitution_nests_one_level_through_a_list` is the deepest the grammar reaches. The counter is kept anyway: it is the only thing bounding the recursion if the grammar ever gains a way to nest, and removing it would leave a recursion whose depth is set only by the length of a string literal. Recorded in `FINDINGS.md`.

